        {
          "text": "As with anything creative, there are as many ways of writing a joke as there are people doing it. Sometimes a joke will ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 70
        }
      ],
      "words": 58
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "One way of writing cheerfully bad gags is to work backwards",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 373
        }
      ],
      "words": 11
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Start off with a phrase, an idiom, a movie title or something else well-known enough that your audience will know what i",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 455
        }
      ],
      "words": 39
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Think of rhymes, homophones (words that mean different things but sound the same), homonyms (words that mean different t",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 919
        }
      ],
      "words": 57
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Numbers aren’t on your side. There are jokes that are so bad they’re good, and jokes that are so bad they’re really, rea",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1274
        }
      ],
      "words": 39
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Did the Tudors and Stuarts battle over who had the most attractive nostrils in the Phwoar of the Noses? Doubt it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1666
        }
      ],
      "words": 21
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Now build out a setup, ideally not using any of the key words from the punchline. This might be a simple question: what ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1807
        }
      ],
      "words": 46
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There’s a fairly well-known punchline, ‘Super calloused fragile mystic vexed by halitosis’, which can be reached in a lo",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2257
        }
      ],
      "words": 21
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Think about whether your joke is just confusing. You’ve been there for the whole process, but put yourself in the shoes ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2579
        }
      ],
      "words": 36
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "For instance, ‘What’s a farmer’s favourite 1980s action film? The Germinator!’ is a play on the word ‘germinate’, which ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2775
        },
        {
          "text": "It’s a confusing old mess really – not a joke as much as a noise. Probably best to ditch it and start again",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3064
        }
      ],
      "words": 70
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Have you finally come up with one that just about works? Well done! Now write another hundred",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3192
        }
      ],
      "words": 17
    }
